{"base_rate":0.08869565217391304,"brier":0.07912886956521739,"bss":0.02103044080227512,"bss_hi":0.25357799185098273,"bss_lo":-0.34087437938444304,"country":"TR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.07055652173913043,"ess":274.0823783424682,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Mersin</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Mersin rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (77%), believe about\n<b>45%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 575 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-17. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMERSIN, 1.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.02, ranked 106 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(75&ndash;108) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>321</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'><b>13%</b></td><td class='num'>52</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Mersin</b> <span class=\"muted\">TR</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.02</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>75&ndash;108\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>575 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Mersin &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Mersin\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 70.8325,354.58625000000063 94.21692307692308,312.0 153.96718750000002,239.8125 329.2372413793103,68.20689655172418 329.2372413793103,137.24137931034483 153.96718750000002,319.4375 94.21692307692308,375.0 70.8325,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"349.71478260869566\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"349.71478260869566\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,372.9283489096573 70.8325,363.8 94.21692307692308,333.0 153.96718750000002,347.875 329.2372413793103,218.82758620689654\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 321 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"372.9283489096573\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"70.8325\" cy=\"363.8\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 10%&amp;#10;It rained 13% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 52 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"94.21692307692308\" cy=\"333.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 27%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"153.96718750000002\" cy=\"347.875\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 77%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 58 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"329.2372413793103\" cy=\"218.82758620689654\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(9%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Not enough days in this city's record to split the year into four and still say anything defensible about each part. The split is shown only where it is supported.</p>\n"},"lat":36.81196,"lon":34.63886,"n":575,"n_cities":109,"name":"Mersin","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":321,"obs":0.024922118380062305,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.